course: dictionary
lesson: 14881
title: Recharge
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To recharge means to fill something up with energy again. A phone runs out of power, so you plug it in to recharge it. «My tablet is flat, so I need to recharge it now.» Flat means it has no power left.
explain: You can also recharge yourself. When you feel tired, a quiet rest helps you get your energy back. «After school I like to lie on the sofa and recharge.» Here recharge does not mean electricity. It means resting until you feel strong again.
explain: The same word works for both. Ask yourself: is a battery running out of power, or is a person tired? The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning in and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Recharge means to fill something with electricity again, or to get your energy back by resting.
fact: «Rechargeable» batteries can be used again and again, because you plug them in to recharge them.
fact: «Recharge the battery» means put more power into it.
fact: «Recharge your batteries» is a way of saying rest so that you have more energy.
fact: «A recharge» is a noun: «I need a recharge after a busy week» means you need a rest to get your energy back.
exercise: «My phone is nearly flat, so I will plug it in to recharge.» What does recharge mean here? | To drop it on the floor | To turn it into a bag | To sing loudly | *To fill it with power again
exercise: «After the long weekend, I felt fully recharged.» What does fully recharged mean? | Covered in water | *Full of energy again after resting | Still very tired | Missing a battery
exercise: Which sentence uses recharge to mean rest and get your energy back? | *«I lie on the sofa to recharge after school.» | «The charger is in the drawer.» | «The lamp needs a new plug.» | «The battery is flat, so recharge it.»
test: «Rechargeable batteries can be used again.» What does rechargeable mean? | Only used once | *Able to be filled with electricity again | Made of wood | Very loud
test: What does «a recharge» mean in «I need a recharge after a busy week»? | *A rest that gives you energy back | A loud noise | A wet day | A sharp pencil
exam: Ella says, «My laptop is at 2 percent, so I must recharge it before the bus.» What must Ella do? | Ask the bus driver for a new laptop | Read a book about buses | *Plug the laptop in to fill its battery | Put the laptop in the bin
